The natural bent-function family fails Track A because deterministic algebraic constructions produce witnesses directly. A Track B Walsh-spectrum reconstruction variant was also tested, but all 9/9 oracle attempts solved it across \(n=6,8,10\). At \(n=10\), the compact solution needs only 192 sign operations; increasing further violates G9’s 300-operation cap.

The official hardening verdict was `too_easy`. Per the task’s rejection rule, no generator or shipping artifacts were retained. The audit records the paper analysis, gate measurements, algorithms, and all oracle results. See the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.08706).
